INT. FUNICULAR CAR MIDWAY UP A MOUNTAIN - NIGHT

A wooden cable car, stopped dead on a steep track. Wind rattles the windows. Below, a hotel's lights glitter in the valley.

REUBEN FAIRCHILD, forties, gray tuxedo, kneels by a floor panel with a pry bar. KASIMIR VOSS, thirties, black tuxedo, holds a flashlight and watches the track behind them. Each wears a small earpiece.

KASIMIR
Cable's steady. We have maybe six minutes.

REUBEN
Four, if she's right.

He pries the panel. It lifts. Beneath it, a steel lockbox bolted to the frame.

ODALYS (V.O.)
(in their earpieces, calm)
Gentlemen, the hotel's night manager just left his office. He's walking to the lift station.

KASIMIR
How long to get here?

ODALYS (V.O.)
Walking? Ten minutes. If he notices the car's stopped, he'll run.

REUBEN
Then let's not make him notice.

Reuben takes a thin case from his jacket and opens it. Lockpicks, a stethoscope. He hangs the stethoscope around his neck and presses the diaphragm to the box.

KASIMIR
You said it was a four-digit lock.

REUBEN
It's a six-digit lock.

KASIMIR
You said four.

REUBEN
I said four minutes.

Kasimir lets that go. He turns the flashlight off. Darkness, then the pale blue of mountain night.

ODALYS (V.O.)
I'm watching the manager. He's stopped. He's looking up at the track.

KASIMIR
Stopped?

ODALYS (V.O.)
Stopped. Pulling out a phone.

Reuben's hands freeze on the dial. Kasimir leans toward the window, one hand on his gun.

REUBEN
Odalys. Is he calling the lift station?

ODALYS (V.O.)
Hold on.

A long silence. Wind. The car creaks. Reuben's breath fogs the glass.

KASIMIR
(whispering)
He's seen the car. He knows.

REUBEN
He doesn't know.

KASIMIR
He has a phone in his hand.

REUBEN
He has a phone. That's all he has.

Reuben turns the dial again. A click. Another.

ODALYS (V.O.)
He's dialing. Oh, he's dialing the front desk, not the lift. The front desk.

KASIMIR
That's a different thing?

ODALYS (V.O.)
It's a sleepy clerk with a cold. That's a very different thing.

Click. Click. Reuben's face. The lock drops. He lifts the lid.

Inside, a velvet pouch. He opens it. A stone the size of a plum catches the blue light.

KASIMIR
That is the ugliest diamond I have ever seen.

REUBEN
It's a spinel. Worth three diamonds.

ODALYS (V.O.)
Boys, the manager's put the phone away. He's shrugging. He's walking back to the hotel.

Kasimir lets out a laugh he's been holding. Reuben closes the lid, slides the pouch inside his coat, drops the panel back into place.

KASIMIR
And that's it?

REUBEN
That's it.

The car lurches. Starts to move again, upward, humming.

ODALYS (V.O.)
Somebody just turned the power back on. You've got ninety seconds to the top station.

KASIMIR
Ninety seconds to look like we belong at a gala.

Reuben straightens his bow tie. Kasimir slicks his hair. The car glides on up the mountain toward the lights.

REUBEN
Nobody ever looks at the men in the funicular.

ODALYS (V.O.)
I'm looking at you.

REUBEN
Nobody but you.
